    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Understanding Positional Embeddings in Modern LLMs",
      "url": "https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/p/understanding-positional-embeddings",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50506376",
      "score": 183,
      "comments": 23,
      "author": "vismit2000",
      "published": "2026-11-15T12:14:06Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE) dominate modern architectures like LLaMA and Mistral, encoding relative distance directly via 2D query/key vector rotations.",
        "ALiBi injects linear biases into attention scores based on token distance, offering robust zero-shot length extrapolation without learned positional parameters.",
        "Context extension relies on RoPE interpolation techniques like NTK-aware scaling and YaRN to mitigate out-of-distribution frequency collapse at high sequence lengths."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "All AI-generated code should be Open Source",
