      "score": 24,
      "comments": 9,
      "author": "Yogthos",
      "published": "2026-11-15T16:04:01Z",
      "bullets": [
        "US copyright rulings deny authorship to non-humans, legally pushing unassisted synthetic output into the public domain by default.",
        "Models trained on copyleft repositories risk license contamination when emitting verbatim GPL code directly into proprietary software projects.",
        "Engineering teams require robust provenance tracking and SCA tooling to detect untracked synthetic code and mitigate IP exposure."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Blog: Preventing Cross-Service UDP Loops in QUIC",
      "url": "https://bughunters.google.com/blog/preventing-cross-service-udp-loops-in-quic",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/om6v89",
      "score": 4,
      "comments": 0,
      "author": "freddyb",
      "published": "2026-11-15T20:34:37Z",
      "bullets": [
        "UDP loop vulnerabilities trigger infinite packet ping-pong between QUIC endpoints and other UDP services exchanging error or reset packets.",
        "Mitigate loops by dropping responses targeting well-known UDP service ports and strictly rate-limiting Stateless Reset and Version Negotiation packets.",
        "Enforce RFC 9000 3x anti-amplification limits and require minimum 1200-byte client datagrams before responding to unverified IP addresses."
      ]
    },
